Story file exists and matches the provided spec: - docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md,Dedicated tests explicitly reference this story and its requirements: - tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts - Header: "* Tests for: docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md" "* @story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md" "* @req REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING ..." "* @req REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT ..." - describe("Auto-fix behavior (Story 008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX)", () => { ... }) - For REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING (missing @story): multiple invalid cases define both input and expected output, e.g.: - Function declaration: code: "function autoFixMe() {}" output: "/** @story docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md */
function autoFixMe() {}" - Function expression, class method, TS declare function, TS method signature all have similar before/after expectations. - For REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT (path suffix normalization): - Adds .md when path ends with .story - Adds .story.md when there is no extension while leaving already-correct paths unchanged.,Implementation of auto-fix for missing @story annotations (REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE): - src/rules/require-story-annotation.ts - Includes traceability to this story: "@story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md" "@req REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING - This rule supports auto-fixing missing @story annotations per Story 008.0 auto-fix behavior." "@req REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE - Auto-fix behavior only inserts @story annotation JSDoc comments and never changes executable or runtime code." "@req REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE - Auto-fix inserts a minimal placeholder JSDoc in a way that preserves existing surrounding formatting and structure." - meta.fixable = "code" (enables ESLint --fix). - create(context) delegates to visitors that call helper functions with fixers. - src/rules/helpers/require-story-helpers.ts - Defines the built-in placeholder template used by fixes: const STORY_PATH = "docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md"; const ANNOTATION = `/** @story ${STORY_PATH} */`; - reportMissing(...) and reportMethod(...): - Guard with hasStoryAnnotation(...) so fixes are only applied when truly missing. - Call context.report with both fix and suggest: fix: createAddStoryFix(resolvedTarget) or createMethodFix(resolvedTarget) suggest: [{ desc: `Add JSDoc @story annotation ...`, fix: createAddStoryFix(...) }] - These functions are annotated with this story and REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING / REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE / REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE. - src/rules/helpers/require-story-core.ts - createAddStoryFix(target): computes a range start for the node (or its export wrapper) and uses fixer.insertTextBeforeRange([start, start], `${ANNOTATION}
`); only a comment line is inserted. - createMethodFix(node): similar but inserts `${ANNOTATION}
 ` before methods. - These helpers do not alter function bodies or other code, only add comments immediately before the target node.,Implementation of auto-fix for annotation format issues (REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE): - src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts - Contains explicit traceability: - For reportInvalidStoryFormat / reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix / validateStoryAnnotation: "@story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md" "@req REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT ..." "@req REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE ..." "@req REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE ..." - meta.fixable = "code" with a doc comment: "This rule's fixable support is limited to safe @story path suffix normalization per Story 008.0..." and tied to this story. - createStoryFix(context, comment, fixed): - Reads the original comment text via sourceCode.getText(comment). - Locates "@story" and then only the value substring using regex, computes a tight [start, end] range. - Returns a factory that uses fixer.replaceTextRange(fixRange, fixed). - Returns null when tag/value cannot be safely located (no fix is attempted). - reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix(...): - If createStoryFix returns null, it falls back to reportInvalidStoryFormat (error only, no fix), satisfying safe behavior for ambiguous cases. - Else calls context.report with fix: fixFactory(). - validateStoryAnnotation(...): - Computes collapsed value; if it matches options.storyPattern, returns (no report). - If value includes whitespace, calls reportInvalidStoryFormat (no fix) to avoid guessing complex values. - Otherwise calls getFixedStoryPath(collapsed). If fixed is non-null and matches pattern, it calls reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix(..., collapsed, fixed); otherwise it reports invalid with no fix. - src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-utils.ts - getFixedStoryPath(original: string): annotated for this story and its auto-fix requirements. - If original includes ".." → returns null (no fix) to avoid path traversal (REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE). - If original already ends with ".story.md" → returns null (no change). - If ends with ".story" → returns `${original}.md`. - If ends with ".md" → replaces with ".story.md". - Otherwise appends ".story.md". - All operations preserve the base path and directory, only normalizing the suffix (REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE).,Documentation describing auto-fix capabilities for users (Documentation acceptance criterion): - user-docs/api-reference.md - traceability/require-story-annotation section: "When run with `--fix`, the rule inserts a single-line placeholder JSDoc `@story` annotation above missing functions, methods, TypeScript declare functions, and interface method signatures using a built-in template aligned with Story 008.0. This template is currently fixed but structured for future configurability, and fixes are strictly limited to adding this placeholder annotation without altering the function body or changing any runtime behavior." - traceability/valid-annotation-format section: "When run with `--fix`, the rule limits changes to safe `@story` path suffix normalization only—for example, adding `.md` when the path ends with `.story`, or adding `.story.md` when the base path has no extension—using targeted replacements implemented in the `getFixedStoryPath` and `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix` helpers. It does not change directories, infer new story names, or modify any surrounding comment text or whitespace, in line with Story 008.0; more advanced path normalization strategies and selective toggles to enable or disable specific auto-fix behaviors are not yet implemented." - These docs match the behavior implemented in the code and the tests, and explicitly mention Story 008.0.,Targeted test execution for this story: - Command run: npm test -- --runInBand --verbose --testPathPatterns tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts - Tool output: "> eslint-plugin-traceability@1.0.5 test
> jest --ci --bail --runInBand --verbose --testPathPatterns tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts" - The tool did not report a command failure for this invocation, indicating Jest executed the specified test file without failing assertions.
